.Dd July 24, 2026
.Dt NIXOS-GENERATE-CONFIG 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nixos-generate-config
.Nd generate NixBSD configuration by inspecting the running system
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -dir Ar directory
.Op Fl -root Ar directory
.Op Fl -force
.Op Fl -no-filesystems
.Op Fl -show-hardware-config
.Sh DESCRIPTION
This command generates an initial NixBSD configuration file
.Pa /etc/nixos/configuration.nix
and a hardware scan file
.Pa /etc/nixos/hardware-configuration.nix .
The latter contains settings determined by inspecting the hardware and
currently mounted filesystems.
This is useful for creating an initial configuration after installing
NixBSD, or when hardware changes have been made.
.Pp
The hardware configuration includes:
.Bl -bullet
.It
CPU architecture detection (x86_64, aarch64)
.It
Virtualization detection (KVM, bhyve, VirtualBox, VMware, etc.)
.It
Mounted filesystem detection with stable device paths
(via /dev/gpt/, /dev/ufsid/, /dev/msdosfs/)
.It
ZFS pool detection
.It
Swap device detection
.El
.Pp
.Pa configuration.nix
is not overwritten if it already exists unless
.Fl -force
is specified.
.Pa hardware-configuration.nix
is always overwritten, since it is generated from the current system state.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl -dir Ar directory
Write the configuration files to
.Ar directory
instead of
.Pa /etc/nixos .
.It Fl -root Ar directory
Treat
.Ar directory
as the root of the target filesystem.
Used during installation when the target is mounted at a subdirectory.
.It Fl -force
Overwrite
.Pa configuration.nix
even if it already exists.
.It Fl -no-filesystems
Skip filesystem and swap detection.
Only hardware attributes will be included in the generated configuration.
.It Fl -show-hardware-config
Print the generated hardware configuration to standard output instead of
writing files.
Useful for inspecting what would be generated.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/etc/nixos/hardware-configuration.nix"
.It Pa /etc/nixos/configuration.nix
Main NixBSD system configuration file.
.It Pa /etc/nixos/hardware-configuration.nix
Auto-generated hardware-specific configuration.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Generate configuration for the currently running system:
.Pp
.Dl # nixos-generate-config
.Pp
Generate configuration for a system mounted at /mnt:
.Pp
.Dl # nixos-generate-config --root /mnt
.Pp
Show what hardware configuration would be generated:
.Pp
.Dl # nixos-generate-config --show-hardware-config
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr nixos-install 8 ,
.Xr nixos-rebuild 8
.Sh AUTHORS
NixBSD Contributors
